/* Hero showcase, tab 4 "Work together on one site": invite a teammate to the site from its Team tab,
   then tag them in a note on the page and read it back in the Comments list.

   The screens are a copy of the live app at 1280 x 696 (cowork.tracy.site, site kinetic-demo, read
   23/10/2026): the app's DOM was walked with each element's computed style and box, and rebuilt here
   as absolutely placed boxes (SCREENS below; their look is the hs4-s* classes in hero-showcase-tab4.css).
   Round 46 (25/10/2026) rebuilt the Team page and the Invite people dialog from tch develop (TeamView.tsx,
   team/wizard-steps.tsx) as real flow HTML (the "Round 46" block of the css file) and re-ordered the story.
   People, their comments and the team are made up; addresses use the reserved .example domain.

   Scenes (ms from the start of the tab; the pace of scene 1: the pointer rests 0.7 s on a target before it
   presses, an overlay opens 0.4 s after the press, each new state is held 1.5 s):
      1. The site in the app, empty: no comments yet.
      2. The Browser tab's site switch, the site's submenu, "Team": the Team page. "Invite member": the Invite
         people dialog; Daniel's address is typed and committed as a chip, Editor, Continue (Sites), Continue
         (Review), "Send invitation", "Invitation sent". Done: the Team list now holds Daniel as Invited.
      3. Back to the site tab, Edit mode: the pointer clicks the headline; the Comment box opens; the note is
         typed, "@" opens the picker, Daniel (now on the team) is picked; "Note for team": the box closes,
         a pin sits on the block and the Comments count reads 1.
      4. "Comments": the thread (the note with @daniel), held; the scene ends there. */
